\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Top Japan MOF official Kuroda going to US, Europe. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yoko Nishikawa \par \uc2 619 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2001\par 13:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 19 (Reuters) - Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said on Wednesday he was sending his ministry's top financial diplomat to Europe and the United States to exchange views on various issues regarding the global economy. \par \par \uc2  Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda would meet his counterparts soon to exchange views as no final decision has been made on when and where Group of Seven (G7) finance ministers should meet after the attacks in the United States, he said. \par \par \uc2  "Given the situation, I will urgently send Kuroda to Europe and the United States to gather information and keep contact," Shiokawa told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether the purpose of Kuroda's trip was to talk about cooperation with other nations in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Shiokawa told a news conference: "Well, there is no special purpose of the trip." \par \par \uc2  Japanese monetary authorities again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday to hold down the yen. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa gave no detailed information on Kuroda's trip, and ministry officials declined to comment on his schedule. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa said he had not received any news on the schedule of the G7 finance ministers' meeting from the United States, which is the host country of the meeting. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the day, several finance ministry officials said Kuroda was to stay in Tokyo on Thursday and there was no plan to hold a meeting of G7 finance deputies in London then, which some G7 sources had suggested was under consideration. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  TO STABLILSE MARKET \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa added that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for yen - which followed similar \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday - was conducted to stabilise the market, where the dollar was falling toward seven-month lows below 117 yen set earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  "While there are worries about global financial markets and stock movements, I would like to avoid any drastic movements. It (the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is conducted reluctantly but we have done so in order to stablise the market." \par \par \uc2  Asked whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in afternoon Tokyo trading, Shiokawa declined to comment directly, but said: "You can find it out from looking at charts" \par \par \uc2  An international monetary source told Reuters at around 0600 GMT that the Bank of Japan was buying dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  REQUESTS ON BOJ \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa also disclosed that Senior Vice Finance Minister Seiichiro Murakami, who attended the Bank of Japan's (BOJ) Policy Board meeting on Tuesday, had asked the board to raise the target for funds flowing from the money market into current account deposits at the BOJ to above eight trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ, joining a global effort to avoid recession after attacks on the United States, announced a set of steps on Tuesday to loosen its already ultra-easy monetary policy, including expanding the current account deposit target to above six trillion yen from "around" six trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also decided it would cut its discount rate, which it charges on its loans to commercial banks, to 0.10 percent from 0.25 percent and it expanded its emergency Lombard lending facility. \par \par \uc2  Government representatives can attend the BOJ policy-setting board meetings but cannot vote on policy decisions. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa also said Murakami had asked the BOJ at Tuesday's meeting to keep funds from the yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "unsterilised". \par \par \uc2  In unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the BOJ leaves the yen funds from its yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said on Wednesday it appeared that at least some of Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unsterilised. \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market settlement takes place two business days after a transaction. \par \par \uc2  (Yoko Nishikawa, Tokyo Newsroom +81-3 3432 7587 \par \par \uc2  tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010919dx9j00g20\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
