\par\par \b \uc2  SGX Nikkei up on BOJ action, Taiwan pares losses. \b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2001\par 09:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 19 (Reuters) - SGX Nikkei futures racked up \par \par \uc2  gains on Wednesday due to a combination of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \par \par \uc2  easier monetary policy and its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  market to stem the yen's appreciation. \par \par \uc2      The December contract gained 290 points to close at 9,925. \par \par \uc2  It had risen to an intraday high of 10,030 before profit taking \par \par \uc2  set in and pared its gains, traders said. \par \par \uc2      The BOJ said after the Tokyo market closed on Tuesday it \par \par \uc2  was boosting its liquidity injections into the banking system. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said it would cut its discount rate to \par \par \uc2  0.10 percent from 0.25 percent. \par \par \uc2      The move came on the heels of rate cuts by the U.S. Federal \par \par \uc2  Reserve and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  a day earlier. \par \par \uc2      The BOJ was also in the market on Wednesday to buy the \par \par \uc2  dollars to curb yen gains. The yen's recent strength, which \par \par \uc2  officials say is not warranted by economic fundamentals, raised \par \par \uc2  concerns about deflation and corporate profitability. \par \par \uc2  "People are quick to take profits above the 10,000 mark. \par \par \uc2  Our charts show that 10,550 is a strong resistance for the \par \par \uc2  Nikkei at the moment," said a trader at a local brokerage. \par \par \uc2      The 10,550 level represents the 38.2 percent retracement of \par \par \uc2  the market's August 2-September 17 downmove. \par \par \uc2      SGX Taiwan futures pared losses after the government \par \par \uc2  stepped in to buy stocks in the cash market, but players lacked \par \par \uc2  the resolve to push it into positive territory. \par \par \uc2      The September contract hit an intraday low of 165.6 before \par \par \uc2  crawling back up to close at 171.2, with 12,649 lots changing \par \par \uc2  hands. U.S. names and one local bank were major sellers. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The highly correlated TAIEX         ended 6.55 points\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par higher -- a 0.17 percent rise -- at 3,718.17.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SGX NIKKEI 225 FUTURES\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Contract      DEC1         DEC1\par  Settlement    9925         9925\par  High         10030        10030\par  Low           9610         9610\par  Prev Close    9635         9635\par  Net Change    +290         +290\par  Volume       19255        19255\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SGX TAIWAN MSCI FUTURES\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Contract      SEP1         OCT1\par  Settlement   171.3        171.8\par  High         171.5        170.5\par  Low          165.6        167.4\par  Prev Close   175.1        175.6\par  Net Change    -3.8         -3.8\par  Volume       12648           12.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010919dx9j007vj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
