\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar vaults as Bank of Japan rides to rescue. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hideyuki Sano \par \uc2 802 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2001\par 08:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 19 (Reuters) - The dollar jumped nearly a full yen in Tokyo on Wednesday after Japanese monetary authorities stepped in for the second time this week to stop the shell-shocked U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from falling below 117 yen. \par \par \uc2  The unilateral action was enough to keep dollar bears in check for now, but dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weak trend would only be reversed if the Bank of Japan was joined by other central banks in a concerted push. \par \par \uc2  "It seems the authorities want to build a psychological barrier at 117 yen. Now they have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice near that level, people will be wary of 117 yen," said Jun Kato, manager at Shinkin \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan started buying dollars for the yen when the greenback threatened to fall to 117 yen in a repeat performance of its Monday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , when the dollar hit a 6-= month low below 117 yen. \par \par \uc2  The action boosted the dollar above 118 yen at one point from an intraday low of 117.10 yen. It later eased slightly to 117.85/00 yen but was still higher than late New York levels around 117.24 yen. \par \par \uc2  The euro also rose to around 108.98/08 yen from 108.50 yen, although the BOJ is said to have bought only the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was slightly easier versus the dollar at 92.50 cents down from late New York levels around 92.73 cents but still above Tuesday lows around 92.05 cents. \par \par \uc2  HELPED BY THIN TRADE \par \par \uc2  With trade still unusually thin in the wake of last week's terror attacks on New York and Washington, dealers said the Bank of Japan had not needed to spend much to achieve its goal. \par \par \uc2  Japan has repeatedly said a strong yen is not in keeping with its flagging economy and Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa vowed on Wednesday to continue to take action when necessary. \par \par \uc2  But most dealers think the Japanese authorities are intent on only blocking the dollar's fall rather than reversing its trend. \par \par \uc2  Hideyuki Tsukamoto, a manager at Fuji Bank, said: "People are getting used to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  now, so if the intention is to change the trend, rather than just calm the market, joint action will be needed." \par \par \uc2  Many players said the dollar was likely to remain under pressure for now, amid worries the attacks would shatter U.S. consumer sentiment and push the weak U.S. economy into recession. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has fallen steadily since last Tuesday's devastating plane attacks, hitting multi-month lows against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Even a concerted round of global rate cuts aimed at heading off a recession failed to give the dollar much support, with dealers saying that the latest easings by the Bank of Japan and the Bank of England has been relatively disappointing. \par \par \uc2  The major U.S. stock indices - which shed around seven percentage points on Monday after the longest trading moratorium since the Great Depression - are set to dictate the greenback's fortunes in the near-term, market observers say. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, a tepid rebound from Monday's slide fizzled and the dollar fell against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in tandem. \par \par \uc2  UNSTERILISED \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not conduct its regular money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, thereby confirming it was not absorbing the yen funds it injected during Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions have to be settled two days later. \par \par \uc2  This so-called unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been advocated by many economists, who say it adds to the impact of the BOJ's monetary easing. \par \par \uc2  But the BOJ has said there is no point questioning whether \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is sterilised or not, because it already provides massive extra funds every day. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think there is any impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said Koji Fukaya, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0310 GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                     Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2000\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Cls\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                              18 Sep.\par                     -----------------------------------------\par   Euro/dlr              0.9250   0.9273   -0.25    -2.59   0.9496\par   Dlr/yen               117.85   117.24   +0.52    +2.97   114.45\par   Euro/yen              109.05   108.78   +0.25    +0.31   108.71\par   Dlr/swiss             1.6004   1.5966   +0.24    -0.05   1.6012\par   Stg/dlr               1.4664   1.4678   -0.10    -2.24   1.5000\par   Can/dlr               1.5713   1.5720   -0.04    +5.36   1.4914\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Aus/dlr 0.4945 0.4968 -0.46 -11.60 0.5594 Euro/swiss 1.4804 1.4814\par -0.07 -2.74 1.5221 Euro/s