\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Shiokawa says  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 fx \highlight\uc2  market alone. \b0\par\par\uc2 288 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2001\par 05:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 19 (Reuters) - Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said on Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted earlier in the day was done by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone. \par \par \uc2  He declined to comment on the scale of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "As I have said before, the ministry will take appropriate action if conditions warranted. Today's move is in line with our stance," Shiokawa told reporters at the Finance Ministry briefly after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in coordination with other countries, he said that all depended on market conditions. \par \par \uc2  The dollar leapt to 118.07 yen from just above 117.00 after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Asked his view on the BOJ's decision to leave assets sold in an unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Shiokawa said: "I understand that the BOJ is moving toward that direction." \par \par \uc2  In sterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the BOJ absorbs all the yen funds it injects, whereas in unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the money is left in the financial system, which can indicate a move toward monetary easing. \par \par \uc2  "I welcome yesterday's action (to ease monetary policy). Given that the BOJ has boosted (the target of current account deposits) to over six trillion yen ($51.16 billion), there is no ceiling any more. \par \par \uc2  "It was not the best move but I think it was appropriate," Shiokawa added. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ said on Tuesday it was boosting its liquidity injection to the banking system by raising the target for funds overflowing from the money market into current account deposits at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to above six trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  It also slashed the largely symbolic official discount rate to a record-low 0.10 percent from 0.25 percent. ($1=117.27 Yen). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010919dx9j001am\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
