\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ c/a deposits Y9.5 trln after Mon  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 260 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2001\par 03:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 19 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current account deposits rose to an estimated 9.5 trillion yen ($80.67 billion) on Wednesday after it left Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilised, market sources said. \par \par \uc2  "We have provided ample funds including those from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a BOJ official told Reuters after the bank refrained from its 0020 GMT regular market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , leaving the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds in the money market. \par \par \uc2  BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami said on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Policy Board meeting that the current account deposits could increase on Wednesday when funds from the dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were settled. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlement takes place two business days after the transaction. \par \par \uc2  Since last Wednesday, following the air attacks on the United States, the BOJ had been providing ample liquidity in the money market by increasing its deposits sharply above its previous target of 6.0 trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  After the regular \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, money traders estimated that the deposits stood at around 9.5 trillion yen, up from Tuesday's 8.06 trillion. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ said on Tuesday it was boosting its liquidity injections into the banking system by raising the target for funds from the money market into current account deposits at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to above six trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  In sterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the BOJ absorbs all the yen funds it injects, while in unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the money is left in the financial system, which can indicate a move toward monetary easing. ($1=117.27 Yen). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010919dx9j000sw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
