\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar holds its ground, awaits BOJ decision. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Isabel Reynolds \par \uc2 745 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2001\par 08:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 18 (Reuters) - The dollar firmed a little against the yen on Tuesday, as traders trod warily amid threats of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) stepped into the market to buy dollars the previous day. \par \par \uc2  The greenback was trading around 118 yen in late afternoon, up a shade on the late New York level around 117.91 despite the nose-dive in the U.S. equity markets, which re-opened for business on Monday following a four-day hiatus. \par \par \uc2  Although it was safely above a 6-1/2-month low of 116.65 reached in Tokyo on Monday, the dollar's topside was limited by exporter sales around the 118 mark. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill on Monday announced his support for Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a stand which will likely keep open the option of further dollar-buying, by the BOJ or even the United States. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said earlier on Tuesday \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not eager to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but would do so if necessary. \par \par \uc2  "The government does not want to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but we will take appropriate action or speak about it if need be," he told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  But with the mood in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market still very uncertain, trade remained thin. \par \par \uc2  There are still questions over the reliability of dollar settlement in the aftermath of last week's devastating attacks. Traders are also keen to find out what will happen in the second day of U.S. equities trading, after Monday's seven-percent drop in the Dow Jones Industrial Average \par \par \uc2  MONETARY EASING MOOTED \par \par \uc2  With the BOJ's regular Policy Board meeting in progress, some traders say the dollar is also supported by expectations of further easing in Japan's monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  A sweeping round of 50-basis-point rate cuts from the U.S. Federal Reserve, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other central banks on Monday were putting pressure on the BOJ to join the global effort to avoid a crumbling of confidence after the attacks. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has revealed it will end its meeting on Tuesday, rather than spreading it out over two days, as is customary. \par \par \uc2  The presence of Economics Minister Heizo Takenaka, who has constantly argued for looser policy since his appointment in the spring, at the meeting would seem to suggest further pressure being brought to bear. \par \par \uc2  "I think the BOJ will act and the most likely option is an increase in the current account reserves at the BOJ," said Shingo Funatsuki, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  marketing head at Citibank. \par \par \uc2  One \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has avoided action since last week is the Reserve Bank of Australia and its inaction has helped drive the Australian dollar below 50 cents for the first time in five months. \par \par \uc2  The euro was bid at $0.9190 in late trade, backing off a six-month high around $0.9335 reached offshore. \par \par \uc2  "The euro has not been bought that much since Monday," said Yasunari Ueno, chief market economist at Mizuho Securities. \par \par \uc2  "I think concerns that capital will escape from the U.S. to Europe have eased, at least for now. The central banks have given first aid," he said. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had lost almost a yen on the previous day's post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  highs to stand at 108.52. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0550GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130GMT. \par \par \uc2  Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2000 Cls \par \par \uc2  17 Sep. \par \par \uc2  ----------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr              0.9190   0.9243   -0.57    -3.22   0.9496\par Dlr/yen               118.13   117.85   +0.24    +3.22   114.45\par Euro/yen              108.63   108.94   -0.28    -0.07   108.71\par Dlr/swiss             1.6162   1.6052   +0.69    +0.94   1.6012\par Stg/dlr               1.4624   1.4655   -0.21    -2.51   1.5000\par Can/dlr               1.5704   1.5698   +0.04    +5.30   1.4914\par Aus/dlr               0.4950   0.5022   -1.43   -11.51   0.5594\par Euro/swiss            1.4859   1.4838   +0.14    -2.38   1.5221\par Euro/stg              0.6282   0.6305   -0.36    -0.68   0.6325.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par .. Debt... Indicators... \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports.. All spots Tokyo spots Europe\par spots Volatilities Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Official rates...\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Diary.......             Top\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par events........\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Diaries........... Diaries Index........ Press Digests.... Polls on G7\par economies.. Reuters Television..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010919dx9i008sq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
