\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar edges down on equity fears, BOJ rate cut. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Robin Shepherd \par \uc2 549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2001\par 13:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 18 (Reuters) - The dollar pared early gains against the euro on Tuesday on nervousness ahead of the Wall Street open and lost ground against the yen after the Bank of Japan followed other central banks in cutting interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Overnight and in early European trading, coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate cuts bolstered dollar sentiment which had improved as U.S. stocks on Monday defied the worst predictions of massive losses on the first day of trading since last week's attacks. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said market concerns were refocusing on the state of the U.S. economy and, above all, the stock markets, which could still hit the dollar hard in the event of big falls. Wall Street's open at 1330 GMT was seen as the key event today. \par \par \uc2  "I would be very surprised if at the end of the day the euro was not stronger against the dollar because we do expect further slippage in the U.S. equity markets," said Arjun Mittal, economist at American Express bank. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Swiss National Bank were among those to cut interest rates on Monday to soothe concerns over sluggish growth after last week's attacks. The BOJ followed suit on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was down by a quarter of a percent against the yen compared with the New York close and hit an intraday low at 117.54 after the BOJ's 15 basis point rate cut. Prior to the rate cut the dollar was flat against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at $0.9225 per euro, around one percent above Tuesday's six-month lows at $0.9330 but well off intraday highs at $0.9189. Reports earlier in the day that Afghanistan's ruling Taliban movement would launch a holy war against the United States if the country was attacked, briefly dented dollar sentiment but had no lasting effect on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  WALL STREET OPEN AWAITED \par \par \uc2  Traders said dealing rooms were anxiously waiting to see how Wall Street performed. \par \par \uc2  "The rate cuts and the fact that stocks did not do as badly as they could have done has probably been the cause of the dollar's rise against the euro but this could all change if it goes pear shaped on Wall Street," said one London based trader. \par \par \uc2  Analysts had expected stock market losses of between five and 10 percent on Monday but, in the event, the blue-chip Dow Jones industrial average shed around seven percent. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2  WATCHES \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Monday to stem the yen's export-crimping strength and traders said markets remained wary of further Japanese action. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said earlier on Tuesday \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not eager to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  but would do so if necessary. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill on Monday announced his support for Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a stand which will probably keep alive talk of the potential for further dollar-buying by the Bank of Japan (BOJ) or even the United States. \par \par \uc2  But with the mood in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market still uncertain, trade remained thin and questions lingered over the reliability of dollar settlement following last week's attacks. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010918dx9i00lxt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
