\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 3-BOJ eases monetary policy, following Fed and ECB. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yoko Nishikawa \par \uc2 767 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2001\par 14:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 18 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan, joining a global effort to avoid recession after attacks on the United States, announced a set of steps on Tuesday to loosen its already ultra-easy monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  The move comes on the heels of rate cuts by the U.S. Federal Reserve and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  a day earlier and was almost immediately followed by an easing by the Bank of England. \par \par \uc2  "This is part of the coordinated move by all the central banks to ensure stability in the financial system," said Mark Tinker, global head of strategy at Commerzbank in London. \par \par \uc2  "They're cutting rates to make sure the financial system doesn't lock up at a time when there's an awful lot of strain being put on it." \par \par \uc2  The BOJ said it was boosting its liquidity injection to the banking system by raising the target for funds overflowing from the money market into current account deposits at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to above six trillion yen ($51 billion). \par \par \uc2  The previous official target was "around" six trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami said the Bank would keep the balance, at least in the near term, at around eight trillion yen - a level which it has maintained since last week's deadly attacks in New York. \par \par \uc2  "We will continue to provide ample funds to the market in a flexible manner. As long as there is the kind of fund demand seen now, we will provide funds to keep the current account deposit at eight trillion yen or more," Hayami told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said it would cut its discount rate, which it charges on its loans to commercial banks, to 0.10 percent from 0.25 percent and it expanded its emergency Lombard lending facility. \par \par \uc2  The period for which banks can roll over Lombard borrowings was extended to 10 days from five during the current reserve maintainance period between September 16 to October 15. \par \par \uc2  SWIFT DECISION \par \par \uc2  Economics Minister Heizo Takenaka, a persistent easing proponent who attended the BOJ policy meeting as a government representative, hailed the move as "swift" and said the BOJ was reaching the limit of orthodox easing measures. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, the BOJ cut short its scheduled two-day policy meeting by a day to make its decision part of a global \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action to restore stability in financial markets and brighten the outlook for a slowing world economy. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut their key interest rates by a half percentage point on Monday, while the Bank of England announced its 0.25-point rate cut less than an hour after the BOJ decision. \par \par \uc2  The concerted monetary easing had cheered up the battered Tokyo stock market on Tuesday, with the benchmark Nikkei average rising more than four percent at one point to come within shouting distance of the psychologically crucial 10,000 level. \par \par \uc2  But, reflecting how fragile confidence in financial markets has become, the Nikkei halved its gains in the closing minutes of trade after reports of bomb threats in Tokyo buildings housing international banks and on news that Afghanistan's ruling Taliban was threatening a holy war against the United States. \par \par \uc2  It has close ties with Osama bin Laden, whom U.S. President George W. Bush has called the prime suspect for last week's aerial attacks. \par \par \uc2  Aside from the mounting worries about global recession after the deadly attacks in New York and Washington, Japan faces a tricky period as companies and banks close their books for the first half of the fiscal year on September 30. \par \par \uc2  Last Friday, just two weeks before the book closings, Mycal Corp, Japan's fourth-largest supermarket chain operator, filed for court protection from creditors, leading to fears that many suppliers and creditor banks could take a hit. \par \par \uc2  Hayami said the easing was partly aimed at ensuring smooth fund settlements going into the September book closing. \par \par \uc2  FUNDS FROM \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Hayami said Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt an "undesirable" rise in the yen, which it said could dampen the fragile economy, was conducted at an appropriate time. \par \par \uc2  He added that the BOJ would provide ample funds, including those from the yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , signalling the use of so-called "unsterilised" \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Hayami said the bank's current account deposits could increase on Wednesday when funds from Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be settled. \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market settlement takes place two business days after the actual transaction. \par \par \uc2  (With additional reporting by Chikafumi Hodo). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010918dx9i00llx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
