\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ likely to follow US, European rate action. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mariko Hayashibara \par \uc2 773 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2001\par 04:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 18 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan (BOJ), already expected to loosen credit policy still further this week, could move as soon as Tuesday following U.S. and European rate cuts overnight aimed at restoring market confidence, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's two-day policy-setting meeting kicks off on Tuesday and even though Governor Masaru Hayami said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not make a monetary policy decision on the first day, markets were on the alert. \par \par \uc2  "Announcing today would be much more effective as it will underscore the BOJ's resolve to show a concerted effort with its American and European counterparts," said Shinji Nomura, chief strategist at Daiwa Securities SMBC. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve cut the key federal funds rate to 3.0 percent from 3.5 percent in a bid to restore confidence in financial markets and the global economy after last week's attacks on the United States. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) quickly followed suit, as did the Bank of Canada, the Swiss National Bank and Sweden's Riksbank - all cutting their benchmark rates by half a point. \par \par \uc2  Aside from the mounting worries about global recession after the deadly attacks in New York and Washington, Japan faces a tricky period as companies and banks close their books for the six months to September 30. \par \par \uc2  Last Friday, just two weeks before the book closings, Mycal Corp, Japan's fourth-largest supermarket chain operator, filed for court protection from creditors, leading to fears that many suppliers and creditor banks could take a hit. \par \par \uc2  "In the shadow of the terror attacks in the United States and Mycal's failure, the BOJ cannot avoid providing stepped-up easing measures," said Jun Ishii, chief fixed income strategist at Tokyo-Mitsubishi Securities. \par \par \uc2  Japan's main stock average, the Nikkei 225 , has fallen below the psychologically significant 10,000 level from above 14,000 shortly after Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi took office in late April. \par \par \uc2  To make matters worse, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has risen as investors are losing confidence in the dollar, which could be a blow to the struggling Japanese economy as a stronger yen makes exports more expensive and less competitive. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday and bought dollars to stem the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 117.65/68 on Tuesday morning, up from a seven-month low of 116.65 yen hit on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Amid growing expectation of further BOJ action, Japan's key 10-year government bond yield fell to a one-month low of 1.32 percent on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  POSSIBLE OPTIONS \par \par \uc2  Japanese interest rates are already near zero and yet demand for virtually free money has remained disappointingly slack, leaving the BOJ with limited policy options. \par \par \uc2  Among the policy alternatives, analysts said the most likely scenario was that the BOJ could raise the target for its cash injections into the money market or cut the official discount rate (ODR) from 0.25 percent to possibly 0.10 or 0.15 percent. \par \par \uc2  The ODR is the lending rate for the standby Lombard-style lending facility. \par \par \uc2  The targeted amount of funds in the BOJ's current account deposits was raised to six trillion yen from five trillion at its last policy meeting on August 14, but the BOJ has already raised the amount to around eight trillion yen since the U.S. attacks. \par \par \uc2  "This is just an emergency rise, so the BOJ could say it will be a constant measure," said Tokyo-Mitsubishi's Ishii. \par \par \uc2  To achieve the target, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could increase its outright Japanese government bond (JGB) purchases to possibly 800 billion yen from 600 billion yen per month, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Another option would be using yen funds from \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of its effort to pump more liquidity into the banking system. Shortly after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for yen on Monday, the BOJ suggested it might not drain yen funds this time. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ never usually states explicity whether or not it has sterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , althoug it has on occasion refrained from draining excess yen liquidity to which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has contributed. \par \par \uc2  But analysts were largely sceptical about the effectiveness of these policy options. \par \par \uc2  "Funds used for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are so small compared to the volume of daily fund supply. This will only have an announcement effect," said Daiwa Securities SMBC's Nomura. \par \par \uc2  "After all, the BOJ seems unlikely to gain anything as it can't do much about interest rates, and there has been no apparent effect after its easing in August." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010918dx9i004xv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
