\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-Global help may put some teeth in a new BOJ easing. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shinichi Kishima \par \uc2 827 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2001\par 12:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 17 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan openly admits its monetary easing is having a limited impact on reviving the sickly economy, but analysts say its two-day policy meeting this week could be a rare chance for it to be more productive. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve is expected to cut interest rates later on Monday to prevent a meltdown in the U.S. stock market, which resumes trade for the first time since last week's deadly attacks in New York. \par \par \uc2  That means a BOJ easing now could be meaningful as part of a concerted effort to prevent a global economic crisis. \par \par \uc2  Compared with a solo BOJ easing, which had been anticipated even before the U.S. attacks, a global monetary easing that might bolster world stocks would be more uplifting for Japan, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "Even if the BOJ eased, there is going to be little direct effect domestically," said Mamoru Yamazaki, head of research at Barclays Capital Japan. \par \par \uc2  "But if European and U.S. markets stabilise as a result of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, that would be positive factor for the Japanese market and economy. I think would probably through such a path that an easing would have a real effect." \par \par \uc2  The task for monetary policy is daunting. \par \par \uc2  Recent data suggested Japan's economy had contracted in the April-June quarter and continued to deteriorate in the following months, while Tokyo stock prices have been plumbing 17-year lows. \par \par \uc2  Friday's bankruptcy filing by the nation's fourth largest supermarket operator Mycal Corp adds to the gloomy mix, with risk that many suppliers and creditor banks taking a hit. \par \par \uc2  Thus an element of surprise is needed for the BOJ to make a difference. \par \par \uc2  Financial markets are well aware that Japanese interest rates are already near zero and yet demand for virtually free money has remained disappointingly slack, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "Even if we get a concerted easing, the issue is sentiment," said Takuji Okubo, senior economist at Goldman Sachs Japan. "Particularly in Japan, there is no more room for ordinary easing and the authorities will have to be creative." \par \par \uc2  LIMITS OF QUANTITATIVE EASING \par \par \uc2  When the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased policy last month, it did so by modestly raising the target for its cash injections into the money market. The targeted amount of funds overflowing into banks' current account deposits was ratcheted up to six trillion yen ($51 billion) from five trillion. \par \par \uc2  But the BOJ has already stepped up its liquidity injection over the past week after the U.S. attacks, pumping in enough funds to hoist the current account balance at around eight trillion yen. Incrementally increasing the target would probably not impress too many people. \par \par \uc2  "If all they do is make the eight trillion yen a formal target, that is going to be very disappointing," said Yasushi Okada, economist at CS First Boston Securities in Tokyo. He said a radical increase in purchases of Japanese government bonds was needed at a minimum. \par \par \uc2  Vincent Musumeci, economist at ABN AMRO in Japan, agreed that increased JGB buying should be considered as the JGB market could see a rise in new supply. He said Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi's government might be forced to increase the volume of its upcoming extra budget to cope with the deteriorating economy. \par \par \uc2  "I think it's likely that they will just push on down the road of increasing JGB purchases to offset what is likely to be a larger-than-expected supplementary budget," he said. \par \par \uc2  UNCONVENTIONAL AVENUES \par \par \uc2  In a slight change of tack, the BOJ on Monday hinted at using so-called unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying it would use yen funds from \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of its effort to pump in more liquidity to the banking system. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ has never stated whether or not it sterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because it monitors surpluses and shortages in the whole money market including other factors, traders say excess yen liquidity to which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  contributed has virtually always been drained via money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But shortly after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for yen on Monday, the BOJ suggested it might not drain yen funds this time. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Japan will provide ample liquidity, using funds including those from \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to ensure smooth settlement and stability in financial markets," a BOJ spokesman said. \par \par \uc2  The amount of funds that could be involved remained uncertain, but Okubo at Goldman said Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have opened the way for other money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  using foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated assets. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ has refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  using foreign assets because the Finance Ministry is in charge of the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. But Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said he thought the BOJ would leave funds from Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, giving a green light to mixing monetary policy and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 . ($1=117.65 Yen). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010917dx9h00lri\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
