\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Mizoguchi: Always In Contact With G7 on  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 193 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2001\par 08:24\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Speaking after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to curb the yen's strength Monday, the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's international bureau said he hopes the market understands the resolve of the Japanese authorities. \par \par \uc2  "I hope the market understands that our stance is unchanged," Zembei Mizoguchi told reporters at the ministry. \par \par \uc2  Asked if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone, Mizoguchi merely said, "Only Tokyo markets are open now," but declined to comment further. \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi said Japan was always in contact with monetary authorities in other G7 countries. \par \par \uc2  He declined to comment on how the finance ministry conducted the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday, saying "I won't comment on how \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is conducted." \par \par \uc2  With the greenback creeping lower all morning amid fears U.S. stock prices will head south when trade reopens later in the day, the Japanese Finance Ministry stepped in at around Y116.85, sending the greenback to as high as Y118.35, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0640 GMT, the dollar was trading around Y117.88. \par \par \uc2  -By Arran Scott, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; arran.scott@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917dx9h02ihp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
