\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen defies weak fundamentals, verbal  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mariko Hayashibara \par \uc2 817 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2001\par 04:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 4 (Reuters) - The yen on Tuesday hit a six-week high against the euro and held close to a three-month high versus the dollar, defying miserable economic fundamentals at home and repeated verbal hints of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Japanese authorities. The latest such hint came from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top financial diplomat, Haruhiko Kuroda, repeating his view that the yen's recent strength was abnormal and that the authorities would take action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the situation warranted. \par \par \uc2  Yen bulls were given some pause for thought by the warning from the vice finance minister for international affairs, though this has been said so many times that it is steadily losing its impact, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Still, the threat was enough to help the euro steady just above six-week lows at 107.48/58 yen , against around 107.70 yen in a quiet offshore session. \par \par \uc2  "At least Japanese market participants are not holding short dollar positions now as they are assuming there will be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at some point," said Kosuke Hanao, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at the Royal Bank of Scotland. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 118.83/88 yen , firming from a low of 118.61 yen in the morning, but dealers say the balance of risks is for a test of 118.45/50 support. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yen's firmness was more apparent in euro/yen trade as the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under pressure. \par \par \uc2  "As the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (ECB) rate cut didn't help the euro very much, bearish sentiment is growing yet again on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Hanao said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers and analysts say a break of support at 107.60 yen per eur is seen as bearish and analysts are targeting a retracement level at 106.50/55. \par \par \uc2  The euro was pressed at $0.9048/53 and threatening an eight-week trendline around $0.9040 as well as last week's low at $0.9024. \par \par \uc2  JAPAN MORE CONCERNED ABOUT STOCKS? \par \par \uc2  Dealers kept pondering at what level the Japanese monetary authorities would finally step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but many participants suspected the authorities would hold back until next week. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said on Sunday he would ask what the U.S. government's position is on the dollar when he meets U.S. Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill later this week. \par \par \uc2  O'Neill and Shiokawa are attending a meeting of the finance ministers of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) in China from September 6 to 9, and they meet again in Tokyo around September 12 during O'Neill's visit to Japan. \par \par \uc2  Another focus is Japan's gross domestic product (GDP) figures for the April-June period, due out on Friday, which are likely to show the economy contracted in the period. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said officials may be focusing on Tokyo share prices rather than specific \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels. \par \par \uc2  "I think Nikkei's break below 10,000 level will be the key to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark Nikkei average was again falling on Monday morning, standing at 10,352.47, down 0.55 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they had spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows related to Japanese repatriation of funds ahead of September 30 book-closings as the Nikkei falls along with global equity markets. \par \par \uc2  "I wonder how big the flows are as this is just half-year book closings, but as many firms can no longer take profits in stocks and government bonds, the only choice left is foreign assets," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  In the near-term, the market will be looking at the U.S. release of the National Association of Purchasing Management (NAPM) survey for August, with markets desperate to see whether it confirms the improvement in manufacturing data reported last Friday. \par \par \uc2  Economists surveyed by Reuters expected the NAPM index to rise to 43.9 in August from 43.6 in July, following a surprising surge on Friday in the Chicago regional NAPM index. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0216 GMT.  All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. \par \par \uc2  close at 2130GMT. \par \par \uc2  Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2000 Cls \par \par \uc2  03 Sep. \par \par \uc2  ----------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr              0.9048   0.9069   -0.23    -4.72   0.9496\par Dlr/yen               118.84   118.74   +0.08    +3.84   114.45\par Euro/yen              107.56   107.70   -0.13    -1.06   108.71\par Dlr/swiss             1.6748   1.6705   +0.26    +4.60   1.6012\par Stg/dlr               1.4518   1.4537   -0.13    -3.21   1.5000\par Can/dlr               1.5508   1.5508   +0.00    +3.98   1.4914\par Aus/dlr               0.5257   0.5266   -0.17    -6.02   0.5594\par Euro/swiss            1.5160   1.5153   +0.05    -0.40   1.5221\par Euro/stg              0.6230   0.6234   -0.06    -1.50   0.6325.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010904dx9400i91\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\p