\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ's Hayami unaware if G7 to discuss yen action. \b0\par\par\uc2 145 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2001\par 09:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 4 (Reuters) - Bank of Japan (BOJ) Governor Masaru Hayami said on Tuesday he had not heard whether there would be a discussion on halting the yen's appreciation at a Group of Seven (G7) finance ministers' meeting in Washington later this month. \par \par \uc2  "I don't know about things that far in advance," he told reporters before a meeting of Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi's top economic advisers, the Council of Economic and Fiscal Policy (CEFP). \par \par \uc2  Asked whether Japan would take cooperative action with the United States to lower the yen, Hayami said: "I'm not saying anything." \par \par \uc2  He added that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  required the understanding of the counterparty nations. \par \par \uc2  A decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is made by the Finance Ministry and executed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the government's behalf. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010904dx9400g7f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
