\par\par \b \uc2  Yen Watchers Still On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Alert; Mkt Choppy Tue \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jamie McGeever \par \uc2 546 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2001\par 14:16\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    LONDON -(Dow Jones)- Despite comments to the contrary Tuesday from\par Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Masaru Hayami, Japanese authorities still look\par poised to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to curb the yen's recent\par strength, market observers say.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  But with U.S. authorities unlikely to take the politically unpopular step of buying dollars in a climate of U.S. economic weakness, the Japanese may have to go it alone. \par \par \uc2  "It's a close call," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi. "But the market's convinced (any potential) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be unilateral. The U.S. can't get involved - it would be a big risk politically for the U.S." \par \par \uc2  "I believe they (the Japanese) will (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) at some time in the not-too-distant future," said Lee Ferridge, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Rabobank International, referring to the Japanese authorities. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the final word on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but few people believe it has metaphorically drawn a line in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market sand. \par \par \uc2  A dollar break below Y118 would trigger further stop-loss selling, however, and this would undoubtedly alarm MOF officials, says BOT Mitsubishi's Halpenny. \par \par \uc2  At 1200 GMT, the dollar was at Y119.45, compared with Y118.75 late Monday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    BOJ Tries To Clarify Hayami Comments\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen has defied all of Japan's gloomy economic fundamentals in\par recent weeks to trade firmly against the dollar and the euro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With the Nikkei stock market plumbing fresh 17-year lows almost by the\par day, repatriation flows from Japanese investors to shore up hefty\par balance sheet losses ahead of the half-year fiscal end on Sept. 30 have\par kept the yen strong.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Commentators generally accept that Japan needs a weaker yen to help\par kick-start exports, boost capital spending, stem the economy's\par deflationary spiral, and generally steer the economy away from\par recession.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday, the yen did weaken in volatile and nervous trading, marked by\par the market's hasty misinterpretation of Hayami's comments.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As noted, Hayami said: "I'm not considering it (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) at all."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But a BOJ spokesman later tried to clarify Hayami's remarks, pointing\par out that all he had intended to say was that any decision to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par was up to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and that coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par would require the approval of other countries.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Mkt Covers Short Dollar Positions Tue\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par This was a likely allusion to the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill will visit Japan later in September\par and is scheduled to meet Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa Sept. 12.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the U.S. economy also needs some relief, which could come from a\par weak dollar boost to exports.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. manufacturers have consistently called for a weaker dollar, and\par wouldn't take kindly to the U.S. Treasury helping bail out Japanese\par exporters over domestic exporters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hayami's remarks triggered covering of large short dollar positions\par Tuesday, even though on the surface they are yen-positive. The apparent\par removal of the prospect of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the main barrier to more yen\par strength in the near term, should boost the yen further.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Jamie McGeever, Dow Jones Newswires; +44-20-7842-9483;\par jamie.mcgeever@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010904dx94001p7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
