\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen in focus on Japan  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  talk, euro slips. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Dhara Ranasinghe \par \uc2 825 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2001\par 14:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 3 (Reuters) - The yen was steady within half a percent of recent three-month peaks against the dollar on Monday as verbal threats of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  were offset by repatriation flows before \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's end-September book closing. \par \par \uc2  The euro, meanwhile, shed half a percent against the dollar and the yen, undermined by Friday's encouraging U.S. manufacturing data and worries over the lagged \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  impact of Deutsche Telekom's recent purchase of U.S. VoiceStream. \par \par \uc2  However, the yen took centre stage as Japan stepped up its bid to cap the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export-denting strength. Vice Finance Minister Toshiro Muto said Japan would take appropriate action if rapid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves were seen, while confirmation his boss will meet the U.S. Treasury Secretary for talks on September 12 helped keep markets on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alert. \par \par \uc2  "With the Japanese authorities becoming more aggressive in their stance, the suggestion is that we are closer to actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mitul Kotecha, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Credit Agricole Indosuez. \par \par \uc2  "As we move closer to next week's meeting, there is a risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but this is likely to be unilateral at this stage." \par \par \uc2  Under new accounting rules, Japanese companies must declare the market value of their investments at the fiscal half-year end. Weak Japanese stocks , which closed at a fresh 17-year low, have added to pressure to bring home foreign funds for balance sheet purposes. \par \par \uc2  At 1140 GMT, the yen was trading around 118.80 per dollar , little changed on the day but within half a percent of Friday's three-month peaks. It stood around 107.80 per euro , within sight of Friday's three-week highs. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trading volumes were thin due to the U.S. Labor Day holiday, thus exaggerating price moves. \par \par \uc2  YEN STRENGTH UNNERVES JAPAN \par \par \uc2  Muto's comments came after remarks on Sunday by Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa who reiterated Japan was in contact with its Group of Seven partners about recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility. \par \par \uc2  Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has added about five percent against the dollar in the past month, fuelling concern in Japan that yen strength will stress the already fragile economy. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa officially talks to U.S. Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill in Tokyo next week but the two could meet later this week at a meeting of finance ministers of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation forum in China. \par \par \uc2  "The yen is the main focus," said Steven Saywell at Citibank. \par \par \uc2  "Repatriation flows are nearing an end and there is a risk that rhetoric from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  could turn into outright \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the yen continues to strengthen." \par \par \uc2  Officials at the Federal Reserve and the Treasury on Friday declined to say whether there had been any G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  discussions. Canada's Finance Minister Paul Martin said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "depends on the circumstances," but he declined to give any clues on whether he thought such action would be a good idea. \par \par \uc2  EURO SHINE FADES \par \par \uc2  The euro softened to day's lows around $0.9065 , down almost two cents from 5-1/2 month highs set on August 22, hurt by a couple of U.S. manufacturing indicators on Friday which beat expectations and stirred hopes recession in industry might be stabilising. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was also some concern that a flowback of shares from Deutsche Telekom's acquisition of U.S. VoiceStream could spur selling of billions of euros against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly dollars. \par \par \uc2  Deutsche Telekom completed its purchase of VoiceStream in May. But former shareholders in the U.S. firm agreed a lock-up provision that prevented them from immediately dumping their newly acquired Telekom shares. \par \par \uc2  A major lock-up period relating to the acquisition expired at the weekend, meaning some 200 million Telekom shares could potentially flow back on to the market. Telekom shares were around 16.27 euros each at the European midsession. \par \par \uc2  Such worries encouraged investors to unwind their long euro positions with little fresh direction expected due to the U.S. holiday. \par \par \uc2  Attention was also seen turning to this week's batch of economic news. \par \par \uc2  The yen could face trouble from Japanese growth data for the second quarter, due on Friday. Median forecasts are for a fall of around 0.8 percent, or 3.3 percent annualised. \par \par \uc2  Such an outcome, coupled with the persistent slide in Japanese stocks would pile pressure on the Bank of Japan to ease yet again when it meets later this month, said analysts. \par \par \uc2  The dollar could face a test of its own, with the U.S. National Association of Purchasing Management survey and the payrolls report for August due for release later this week. \par \par \uc2  "The market now wants to see more evidence of what's happpening to the U.S. economy," said Citibank's Saywell. \par \par \uc2  German jobless data are also due this week along with figures on manufacturing orders and industrial output. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010904dx9300i8i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
