\par\par \b \uc2  Japan's verbal action gives little help to dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 795 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2001\par 12:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 31 (Reuters) - Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top finance officials has done little to push down the yen and help the weakening dollar because pessimism over the U.S. economy is drowning out the noise, dealers said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has found some support, but is still struggling around three-month lows versus the yen despite threats on Friday from Japan's finance minister, Masajuro Shiokawa, and his two deputies to stem the dollar's fall. \par \par \uc2  The yen's rise is unwelcome in Japan amid efforts to carry out structural reforms, with its strength expected to hurt the Japanese economy and its stock market, dealers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  participants know Japan is desperate to step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to help lift the dollar, but the market has been unsure what other Group of Seven (G7) nations think about the dollar's depreciation. \par \par \uc2  "Intensified weakness on Wall Street is clearly harming the dollar," said Takashi Toyahara, fixed-income section manager at Nomura Securities. \par \par \uc2  "At this point, we can feel Japan's caution towards the depreciating dollar, but we still can't feel that kind of tension from (other G7 nations)," he said. \par \par \uc2  As of 1045 GMT, the dollar had fallen to around 118.60/65 yen compared with late U.S. levels on Thursday at 119.45/55 yen. \par \par \uc2  JOINT \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  POSSIBLE? \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa expressed concerns on Friday about the dollar's fall below 119 yen for the first time since early June. \par \par \uc2  "Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs (Haruhiko Kuroda) has been in contact with the G7 on the issue. All the countries are dismayed by it (speculative \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves)," Shiokawa said. \par \par \uc2  "We would like to make (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates) more stable through international cooperation," he added. \par \par \uc2  A German finance ministry spokesman said on Friday that it had had no recent contact with the Japanese authorities over any action to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market speculation. \par \par \uc2  Although the market did not expect any G7 members to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite Shiokawa's call, spreading weakness in global share markets, stemming from souring stocks in the United States, could be a good reason for joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I think (the dollar) is approaching levels where Japanese monetary authorities will have to consider \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because they have been saying that the yen's strength will harm the economy," said Michihisa Tanimoto, general manager at Sumitomo Life Insurance. \par \par \uc2  "Also with the U.S. equity market shaking the global equity market, I won't be surprised if the G7 nations decide to coordinate action to support the dollar to help U.S. stocks, as well as the global equity markets," he said. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the Dow Jones Industrial average of blue-chip stocks sank below the psychologically important 10,000-level for the first time since mid-April. \par \par \uc2  EURO/YEN \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  But most dealers believed solo action by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was more likely than a joint effort with Europe or the United States. \par \par \uc2  Doubts over the stance of the U.S. administration reflect the belief that a strong dollar is hurting manufacturing sectors and thus helping to depress the U.S. economy as a whole. \par \par \uc2  Such a belief intensified after the International Monetary Fund warned earlier in August that the deep U.S. current account deficit raised the potential for a steep fall in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Given the uncertainty of U.S. policy towards the dollar, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may choose to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more indirectly, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The United States thinks that the euro's weakness played a more important role in causing the dollar to rise (over the long term) than the yen's weakness did," Nomura's Toyahara said. \par \par \uc2  "I won't be surprised if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  chooses to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the euro against the yen because it should not directly affect the dollar, and not conflict with the U.S. administration's desires," he said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's eagerness to avoid a possible threat to the U.S. economy through a strong dollar can be sensed in Japanese officials' comments. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda reiterated on Friday that the yen's recent strength against the dollar and the euro was too extreme, adding he wanted European authorities to correct the euro's weakness. \par \par \uc2  "The problem is that the euro is too weak. We would like to see that corrected," Kuroda told reporters. He said the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision on Thursday to cut key interest rates to 4.25 percent from 4.50 percent should help to fix the euro's weakness. \par \par \uc2  While the euro moved steadily in a range from 108 to 110.50 yen in August, the dollar has fallen more than five percent to a low of 118.70 yen on Friday from the month's high of 125.21. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010831dx8v00hab\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
