\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro steady ahead of ECB meeting, yen gets fillip. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 745 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2001\par 12:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 30 (Reuters) - The euro held steady against the dollar on Thursday ahead of a policy meeting from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which many expect to result in a growth-boosting rate cut. \par \par \uc2  With the euro unable to make headway ahead of the rate decision, the yen was the largest mover on the day, gaining a third of a percent against the dollar and the euro as Japanese investors repatriated funds ahead of the fiscal half-year. \par \par \uc2  Expectations are for the ECB to cut its key minimum bid rate by 25 basis points to 4.25 percent, but doubts linger after strong European M3 money supply data this week. \par \par \uc2  "We are still looking for a rate cut but the uncertainty is there. If they don't, the market is going to be quite disappointed," said Stacey Seltzer, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Brown Brothers Harriman. \par \par \uc2  "The market is worried because the ECB has been a serial disappointer. In that case the euro will easily test $0.90 and even the $0.89 level by the end of the day." \par \par \uc2  The euro was steady at $0.9087, little changed from the New York close. Against the yen, it was down a third of a percent at 108.82 having fallen as low as 108.53 in early European trading. \par \par \uc2  The ECB's rate decision is at 1145 GMT, followed by a news conference at 1230 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The dollar recovered marginally from earlier session lows of 119.58 yen to trade at 119.76, down from the New York close above 120. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a possible break of 119.50 would trigger stop-loss orders and open the way to 12-week lows of 119.04 set on Wednesday, then this year's low around 118.26. \par \par \uc2  DOUBTS OVER RATE CUT \par \par \uc2  Most economists anticipate an ECB rate cut despite worries about the strong money supply data, arguing the ECB itself had played down the rise in M3 money supply by saying the figures were inflated by special factors. \par \par \uc2  But some market players, unsettled by the rise in M3, took remarks from Bundesbank President and ECB council member Ernst Welteke as a sign the ECB may refrain from taking action this time. He said on Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's focus was on price stability, not on stimulating growth. \par \par \uc2  The ECB cut rates only once this year. By contrast, the U.S. Federal Reserve has shaved rates seven times so far, bringing the benchmark fed funds rate to 3.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  "As the Fed is coming to the end of its easing, the next round of global monetary easing is going to have to be led by the ECB," said John Kyriakopoulos, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase. \par \par \uc2  The dollar found some support after the closely watched revised second-quarter U.S. gross domestic product (GDP) came in on Wednesday above expectations of zero growth. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. economy grew at its slowest pace in eight years, with GDP growth revised down to a 0.2 percent annual rate from a preliminary reading of 0.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  YEN SHORED UP \par \par \uc2  Analysts said disappointing Japanese data and the Nikkei's tumble to another 17-year low were encouraging Japanese investors to repatriate funds to bolster their balance sheets ahead of half-year book closing in September. \par \par \uc2  Japan's industrial output fell for a fifth straight month in July, slipping 2.8 percent from a month earlier, worse than a median forecast of a 2.4 percent decline in a Reuters survey. \par \par \uc2  "There is lots of talk of Japanese exporters selling dollars and Japanese investors repatriating their interest payments on U.S. Treasuries, " a London-based Japanese bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "But we haven't seen real money flows and I reckon short-term speculators are using this talk as an excuse to liquidate their dollar longs." \par \par \uc2  The latest data from the Chicago Mercantile Exchange showed the net short position on dollar/yen on speculative accounts rose to its highest level since November 1999. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yen was unlikely to extend gains significantly beyond 118 to the dollar without incurring verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda said he saw the current yen level as strange and not good for the Japanese economy, adding it was not reflecting economic fundamentals. This reinforced concerns Japan would be unhappy if the yen strengthened further. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010830dx8u00kul\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
