\par\par \b \uc2  Euro stands still, market braces for ECB rate cut. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 670 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2001\par 05:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 30 (Reuters) - The euro was trapped in tight ranges on Thursday morning in Tokyo as operators refrained from taking fresh positions ahead of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (ECB) policy-setting meeting later in the day, dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The wait-and-see mood spilled over to other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , keeping them locked in a narrow band. \par \par \uc2  The market is expecting the ECB to reduce the key refi rate by 25 basis points to 4.25 percent, but dealers were still unsure as to how the euro would react. \par \par \uc2  The market is closely watching whether strong follow-through euro-buying would take place if rates are actually cut. A lack of convincing bids after a rate cut may spur active long liquidation, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that the euro is standing below $0.91 now indicates the market's doubts about seeing a sharp rally after the actual rate cut," a Japanese city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The market is still long of euros after factoring in a credit easing by the ECB," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  At 0250 GMT, the euro stood at $0.9073/83 against Wednesday's late U.S. level of $0.9099/04. \par \par \uc2  Some operators were concerned that the ECB may refrain from taking action after Bundesbank President and ECB council member Ernst Welteke said on Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's focus was on price stability, and not on stimulating growth. \par \par \uc2  A bigger-than-expected rise in euro-zone M3 money supply data for July also dimmed hopes the ECB might cut interest rates. \par \par \uc2  July M3 money supply rose an annual seasonally adjusted 6.4 percent, compared with expectations of an unchanged figure of 6.1 percent. But the ECB played down the jump, saying it was inflated by investors seeking refuge from volatile stock markets by moving into low-risk, short-term paper. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the euro will come under strong selling pressure should the ECB refrain from acting at Thursday's meeting. \par \par \uc2  "A no-rate-cut would surely disappoint the market and trigger massive euro selling," the city bank trader said. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro edged down as yen-buying from exporters in the dollar/yen weighed on the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It was at 108.89/99 against Wednesday's 109.22/33. \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR STILL WEIGHED \par \par \uc2  The dollar was pressured on the yen but short-covering demand and buying from Japanese retail investors limited sharp falls, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The greenback managed to regain some support after the closely watched revised second-quarter U.S. gross domestic product (GDP) came above expectations of zero growth. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. economy grew at its slowest pace in eight years, with GDP growth revised down to a 0.2 percent annual rate from a preliminary reading of 0.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar struggled to rise against the yen, showing muted reaction to a slew of yen bearish factors on Thursday, such as the weaker-than-expected Japanese output figures and continued falls in Tokyo share prices. \par \par \uc2  Japan's industrial output fell for a fifth straight month in July, slipping 2.8 percent from a month earlier, worse than a median forecast of a 2.4 percent decline in a Reuters survey of 13 economists conducted last week. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda also tried to talk down the yen, but the market showed little reaction. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda said he saw the current yen level as strange and not good for the Japanese economy, adding that it was not reflecting economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  But wariness about possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was there, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In offshore trade on Wednesday, the dollar dropped as low as 119.08 yen after breaking below key technical support of 119.70 yen, but rumours of a BOJ rate check induced active short-covering around the lows, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 120.00/10 yen against Wednesday's U.S. close of 120.11/21 yen. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010830dx8u00fh3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
