\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar steady against euro, spotlight on Fed. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Dhara Ranasinghe \par \uc2 701 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2001\par 14:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 21 (Reuters) - The dollar was steady against the euro on Tuesday, hugging a tight range ahead of a U.S. rate decision, but it fell against the yen after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to rule out any near-term \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap yen strength. \par \par \uc2  The yen outshone other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rising over one percent against the euro, as the Japanese Finance Minister's comments damped talk of imminent action to curb the yen's export-crippling strength. But dealers said trade was very thin, thus exaggerating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves. \par \par \uc2  The spotlight was firmly on the Fed, which is widely tipped to trim its key lending rate by 25 basis points although the market is also alert to the possibilty of a bigger cut. Trade is expected to stay thin ahead of the decision due at 1815 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "There is no doubt the main focus today is the FOMC decision," said Neil MacKinnon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Merrill Lynch in London. \par \par \uc2  "In the absence of any key economic releases, the market will be positioning itself for a rate cut this evening." \par \par \uc2  At 1138 GMT, the dollar was trading around $0.9135 per euro, hardly changed on the day and more than half a percent above five-month troughs tested a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  It was pinned near the day's lows around 119.60 yen, down nearly one percent on the day, while the euro was even weaker against the yen around 109.20 yen, down more than one percent on the day. \par \par \uc2  WAITING FOR THE FED \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll showed all 25 primary dealers, who work directly with the Fed in fixed income markets, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would cut its federal funds target for short-term interest rates a quarter point to 3.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  Still, analysts said a larger cut could not be ruled out as there were still no convincing signs of a U.S. economic rebound. \par \par \uc2  They said the dollar's likely reaction to a bigger cut was difficult to call. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  might rally as U.S. equities respond favourably to lower borrowing costs, but it might fall on the combination of a lower yield and fears that the Fed knows of more bad economic news to come. \par \par \uc2  Attention was also seen falling on the Fed's policy statement for clues to the prospects for further rate reductions in the months ahead. \par \par \uc2  So far this year, the Fed has cut rates by a total of 2.75 percentage points to 3.75 percent, taking U.S. rates to their lowest in over seven years. \par \par \uc2  "The statement will be very important for equities and bonds and therefore the dollar," said Jesper Dannesboe, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein. \par \par \uc2  "The first few rate cuts were generally supportive for the dollar as they supported equities and corporate bonds. But the situation has changed, equities are trending lower and corporate bond yields are narrowing." \par \par \uc2  YEN TALK \par \par \uc2  Despite his initial comments suggesting \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not considering \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa later said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) might act if \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves were too "rapid" and even raised the spectre of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Haruhiko Kuroda also weighed in, warning that the ministry was watching the market closely and stood ready to act as needed. \par \par \uc2  "The comments from Shiokawa suggesting they are in no rush to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave the yen a bit of support," said Francesca Fornasari, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Lehman Brothers in London. \par \par \uc2  "But things are very quiet, everyone is simply waiting for the FOMC." \par \par \uc2  The euro, meanwhile, was steady on news the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allocated 83.0 billion euros in 14-day refinancing agreements at 4.50 percent and above for a weighted average rate of 4.51 percent, unchanged from last week's allocation. \par \par \uc2  The rates were bang in line with the results of a Reuters poll of money market dealers on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also little changed after inflation data from 12 key Italian cities suggested Italy's annual inflation rate slowed to 2.8 percent in August from 2.9 percent the previous month, as expected. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dx8l046s6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
