\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar steady against euro as focus turns to Fed. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Dhara Ranasinghe \par \uc2 694 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2001\par 11:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 21 (Reuters) - The dollar was steady against the euro on Tuesday, hugging a tight range ahead of the U.S. rate decision but fell against the yen after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to rule out any near-term \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength. \par \par \uc2  The yen notched up gains of around half a percent against the dollar and euro after Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said he was not considering \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets now, damping talk that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may take imminent action to curb the yen's export-crippling strength. \par \par \uc2  However, the market spotlight was firmly on the U.S. Federal Reserve and dealers said trading conditions were very thin ahead of the interest rate decision at 1815 GMT. The key lending rate was widely expected to be trimmed by 25 basis points but traders were alert to the possibility of a bigger cut. \par \par \uc2  "There is no doubt the main focus today is the FOMC decision," said Neil MacKinnon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Merrill Lynch in London. \par \par \uc2  "In the absence of any key economic releases, the market will be positioning itself for a rate cut this evening." \par \par \uc2  At 0936 GMT, the dollar was trading around $0.9135 per euro, little changed on the day and more than half a percent above recent five-month troughs. \par \par \uc2  It stood around 120.25 yen, down about a third of a percent on the day, while the euro traded around 109.80 yen, down more than half-a-percent on the day. \par \par \uc2  ALL EYES ON FED \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll showed all 25 primary dealers, who work directly with the Fed in fixed income markets, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will cut its federal funds target for short-term interest rates a quarter point to 3.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said a larger cut could not be ruled out as there were still no convincing signs of an economic rebound. \par \par \uc2  They added that the dollar's reaction to a bigger cut was difficult to call. While the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  might rally as U.S. equities responded favourably to lower borrowing costs, the combination of a lower yield and fears the Fed knew of more bad economic news to come might push the greenback down. \par \par \uc2  "The market perceives a 25 basis point cut as the expected action, but there is a very good chance of a 50 bps cut," said Bobby Jasper, senior trader at Fuji Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "There are unlikely to be any fundamental moves in the dollar ahead of the Fed decision." \par \par \uc2  Attention was also seen falling on the Fed's policy statement for clues on the prospects for further rate reductions in the months ahead. \par \par \uc2  So far this year, the Fed has cut rates by a total of 2.75 percentage points to 3.75 percent, taking U.S. rates to their lowest in over seven years. \par \par \uc2  "Given that markets are anxious about the U.S. economy, if the Fed warns risks to the economy are on the downside, it will be difficult for the dollar to make a sustained recovery against this backdrop," said Merill Lynch's MacKinnon. \par \par \uc2  JAPANESE JAWBONING \par \par \uc2  Despite his initial comments suggesting \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not considering \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Shiokawa later said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) might act if \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves were too "rapid" and even raised the spectre of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Haruhiko Kuroda also weighed in, warning that the ministry was watching the market closely and stood ready to act as needed. \par \par \uc2  "The comments from Shiokawa suggesting they are in no rush to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave the yen a bit of support," said Francesca Fornasari, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Lehman Brothers in London. \par \par \uc2  "But things are very quiet, everyone is simply waiting for the FOMC." \par \par \uc2  The euro, meanwhile, was steady on news the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allocated 83.0 billion euros in 14-day refinancing agreements at 4.50 percent and above for a weighted average rate of 4.51 percent, unchanged from last week's allocation. \par \par \uc2  The rates were bang in line with the results of a Reuters poll of money market dealers on Monday. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dx8l0425d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
