\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen held down by Japan's  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  warnings. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Dhara Ranasinghe \par \uc2 645 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2001\par 12:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 17 (Reuters) - The yen was steady about one percent below this week's 2-1/2 month peaks against the dollar, held back on Friday as Japanese officials threatened possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap strength in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Senior Japanese Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi said movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets had been speculative and excessive, following the yen's recent sharp rally. The yen has racked up gains of about five percent against the dollar so far this month. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda added his voice to the warnings, saying that recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves were "not normal" and failed to reflect economic fundamentals. News, meanwhile, that Kuroda had cut short his summer holiday to return to Tokyo heightened tension, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "We have seen jawboning from Japanese officials and this is giving the dollar some support," said Nick Stamenkovic, senior strategist at Nomura International in London. \par \par \uc2  "The last thing the Japanese economy needs is a strong yen, especially after the Bank of Japan cut rates so recently." \par \par \uc2  At 0940 GMT, the dollar was trading around 120.40 yen , steady on the day and around 1-1/2 yen above lows hit on Wednesday. The euro also breached the 110 yen level for the first time since Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  TALKING DOWN THE YEN \par \par \uc2  Kuroda has already warned that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) stood ready to take appropriate action, a standard phrase that has often preceded \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past. \par \par \uc2  Minutes of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy board meeting on July 12-13 showed some members of the board said it was appropriate to allow the yen to weaken as long as it was the result of market mechanisms. The yen was trading at much weaker levels close to 125 per dollar a month ago. \par \par \uc2  Sharp losses in Japanese stocks also kept markets edgy about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen and bolster exporters' competitiveness, dealers said. The Nikkei share average fell to a fresh 16-year low at 11,445.54 points. \par \par \uc2  "The MOF is saying the move is not consistent with fundamentals," said Steven Saywell, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank. \par \par \uc2  "It is unlikely we would get \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at these levels, but I expect increasing rhetoric over the coming weeks." \par \par \uc2  Analysts surveyed by Reuters earlier this week put the probability the Bank of Japan would step in to weaken the yen before the end of September at 30 percent. The likely dollar/yen level was 117, the poll showed. \par \par \uc2  Traders said dollar/yen was also affected by merger and acquisition-related trades. These were rumoured to be related to Furukawa Electric Co's purchase of Lucent Technologies' fibre-optics business, and to Fuji Bank's sale of its stake in Heller Financial in the United States. \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR EYES DATA \par \par \uc2  The euro stood around $0.9130 , up a touch on the day but more than half a percent below Thursday's five-month peaks just above $0.92. \par \par \uc2  Favourable U.S. inflation and housing data accelerated the euro's pullback in early U.S. trading on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar was undermined by a dismal economic report from the Philadelphia Federal Reserve. \par \par \uc2  The Philly Fed's main business conditions index dived to minus 25.3 in August from minus 12.2 the month before, way below analysts' forecasts. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone is looking to sell the dollar on rallies," said a London-based trader. "We are in the early throes of a sea-change for the dollar." \par \par \uc2  The market was now awaiting U.S. trade data for June and the University of Michigan sentiment survey for August later on Friday to offer fresh direction for the dollar, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "If the Michigan survey shows a further fall in confidence, this would clearly weigh on the dollar," said Stamenkovic at Nomura International. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010818dx8h009vl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
