\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar wins reprieve for now, eyes consumer data. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hideyuki Sano \par \uc2 645 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2001\par 08:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 17 (Reuters) - The dollar won a reprieve on Friday after Japanese officials stepped up their warnings on the greenback's recent rapid fall and threatened possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Senior Japanese Finance Ministry (MOF) official Zembei Mizoguchi said movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets had been speculative and excessive. \par \par \uc2  News that the MOF's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief, Haruhiko Kuroda, had cut short his summer holiday to return to Tokyo heightened tension. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda has already warned that the ministry stood ready to take appropriate action, a standard phrase that has often preceded \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were hearing talk that \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely until the dollar fell to 115.00 yen, but some dealers thought the MOF might try to defend 118.30, the low from which the dollar was last pulled back in June. \par \par \uc2  "The government is desperate to stop deflation so the Bank of Japan eased its monetary policy. But the recent appreciation of the yen has offset such efforts. So the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the yen falls below 118 yen," said Naoto Ohnuma, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Mitsubishi Corp. \par \par \uc2  Such a threat was enough to keep the dollar supported at 120.20 yen , some way above the week's 119.05 trough and in line with 120.36 in New York's late trade on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "Japan is facing the worst scenario of a strengthening yen and falling stock prices. So it is natural to think the MOF is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Ohnuma added. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bellwether Nikkei share average fell to a fresh 16-year low at 11,445.54, down 0.60 percent on the day. \par \par \uc2  Traders said dollar/yen was also sandwiched between mergers and acquisitions-related bids at 119.50 and offers around 120.50. \par \par \uc2  The former was rumoured to be related to Furukawa Electric Co's purchase of Lucent Technologies' fibre-optics business, and the latter to Fuji Bank's sale of its stake in Heller Financial in the United States. \par \par \uc2  EURO FLAT \par \par \uc2  The euro was taking time out at $0.9120 having rallied five percent in little more than a week. \par \par \uc2  It took a peek above 92 cents in New York but traders found that rumoured stop-loss buy orders were in fact just rumours and they quickly took profits. \par \par \uc2  Favourable U.S. inflation and housing data accelerated the pullback and saw the euro as low as $0.9090 at one point. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar was rocked anew by a dismal economic report from the Philadelphia Federal Reserve. \par \par \uc2  The Philly Fed's main business conditions index dived to minus 25.3 in August from minus 12.2 the month before, way below analysts' forecasts. \par \par \uc2  The market is now awaiting U.S. consumer confidence and trade data later on Friday to offer fresh direction for the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The market is nervous about dollar-negative factors, so the dollar is still vulnerable," Ohnuma of Mitsubishi Corp said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0606 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                      